<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="027" project="sdap-SPE-admin-app-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Container-type owner management via fileStorageContainerType.permissions</title>
    <phase>3 Workstream C — Correct the API surface</phase>
    <gate>011 complete, 020 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in the BFF Graph hot path plus endpoints and UI; permission-management surface; tags include bff-api and authorization.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Well-specified CRUD against a documented Graph relationship; auth shape already settled by task 011.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W11</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies SpeAdminGraphService.cs. One GraphService task per wave — plan.md §3.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>011, 020, 040</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, authorization, frontend, fluent-ui, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-7 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Adopt the fileStorageContainerType.permissions relationship to manage container-type owners (up to three). This supersedes part of the current ContainerTypePermissions screen.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Graph permission relationships and Fluent UI v9. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>Container-type owners can be listed, added, and removed against Spaarke Dev, with the three-owner limit enforced in the UI.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-C09 / §4.3. The permissions relationship is new and supersedes part of the existing ContainerTypePermissions screen — so this is partly a replacement, not purely an addition. The SharePoint admin center allows up to three owners for settings and billing; the UI must model that limit rather than letting a fourth add fail at the API.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeAdminGraphService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/SpeAdmin/ContainerTypePermissionEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/SpeAdmin/ContainerTypePermissionDto.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpeAdminApp/src/components/container-types</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">Delegated auth — permission management requires it.</dependency>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">v1.0 endpoints.</dependency>
      <dependency task="040" status="pending">WireMock fixture.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: supersession. Determine what the existing ContainerTypePermissions screen still does that the permissions relationship does NOT cover, and keep only that. Do not leave two overlapping owner surfaces — CLAUDE.md §11 points against it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the three-owner limit. Enforce it in the UI with a real message at the limit. A fourth add MUST NOT be offered and then fail at the API.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: destructive operations. Removing the last remaining owner is potentially irreversible — require explicit confirmation and warn about the consequence.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: failure paths. Errors surface as ProblemDetails with the real Graph error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Scope: the owner-management UI. Fluent v9 semantic tokens; dark-mode correct.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this BFF change. Placement Justification in the PR; verify publish size.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Graph container-type permissions relationship</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>knowledge/sharepoint-embedded/docs/learn-containertypes.md</file>
      <file>projects/sdap-SPE-admin-app-r2/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="graph-sdk-v5" location=".claude/patterns/auth/graph-sdk-v5.md">Relationship navigation and writes.</pattern>
      <pattern name="endpoint-definition" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md">Minimal API endpoint shape.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL. Load spec §4.3.</step>
    <step order="1">Audit the existing ContainerTypePermissions screen; record what the permissions relationship supersedes and what it does not.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement list / add / remove against fileStorageContainerType.permissions.</step>
    <step order="3">Enforce the three-owner limit in the UI with a real message at the limit.</step>
    <step order="4">Add confirmation and a consequence warning for removing the last owner.</step>
    <step order="5">Retire the superseded portion of the old screen so only one owner surface remains.</step>
    <step order="6">Add WireMock coverage for list/add/remove request shapes.</step>
    <step order="7">Build BFF and code page; run tests.</step>
    <step order="8">Verify against Spaarke Dev: add and remove an owner successfully.</step>
    <step order="9">Measure publish size; record. Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 027 → ✅. Document deviations in notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If retiring the superseded portion of the old screen would remove a capability the permissions relationship does not provide, STOP and escalate — losing an existing capability is a scope decision, not a cleanup side effect.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>ContainerTypePermissionEndpoints.cs and ContainerTypePermissionDto.cs already exist for the current permissions screen.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — extend the existing permission surface onto the new Graph relationship and retire the superseded portion. No parallel owner-management surface is created.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Container-type owners cannot be managed from the app at all; an admin must use the SharePoint admin center or PowerShell for an operation the tool claims to cover.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Owner add and remove">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a container type's owners</step>
        <step>Add an owner, then remove it</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Both operations succeed and the list reflects each change.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Three-owner limit enforced">
      <steps><step>With three owners assigned, attempt to add a fourth</step></steps>
      <expected>The add affordance is unavailable or blocked with a message naming the limit. No API call is made that would fail.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Last-owner removal warns">
      <steps><step>Attempt to remove the only remaining owner</step></steps>
      <expected>An explicit confirmation appears warning of the consequence before the removal proceeds.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance">
      <steps><step>Toggle dark mode and inspect the owners UI</step></steps>
      <expected>Fluent v9 semantic tokens per ADR-021; no hex literals.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build the SpeAdminApp code page</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Graph/SpeAdminGraphService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/SpeAdmin/ContainerTypePermissionEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/SpeAdmin/ (permissions coverage)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Owners can be listed, added, and removed against Spaarke Dev.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given three owners, when a fourth add is attempted, then the UI blocks it with a message naming the limit.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the last owner, when removal is attempted, then an explicit confirmation with a consequence warning appears first.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Only ONE owner-management surface remains; the superseded portion of the old screen is retired.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an unauthorized caller attempting to add an owner receives 403 ProblemDetails naming the required permission.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: adding an owner that does not exist returns the real Graph error, not a silent no-op.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build 0 errors; tests green; publish size within ceiling.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-C09.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
